Policy: Gates

Purpose:
  Defines gate engine policy, lifecycle, and adaptive gate selection.

Lifecycle:
  REQUIREMENT → BDD → IMPLEMENTATION → STATIC QUALITY → UNIT TEST →
  INTEGRATION TEST → E2E/UI → SECURITY → PERFORMANCE → INFRASTRUCTURE →
  REVIEW → RELEASE → DEPLOY → RUNTIME VERIFY

GateSchema:
  Every gate MUST define:
    id: GATE-<ID>
    condition: <what must be true>
    evidence: <artifact reference>
    threshold: <pass/fail criteria>
    owner: <who validates>
    decision: PASS / FAIL / BLOCKED

GateStatuses:
  PENDING, RUNNING, PASSED, FAILED, BLOCKED, SKIPPED, WAIVED, EXPIRED

GateSeverity:
  BLOCKER, CRITICAL, HIGH, MEDIUM, LOW, INFO

AdaptiveGates:
  Principle: Not all stages are mandatory for all projects.
  Selection factors:
    - Project Level (L0-L5)
    - Technology
    - Risk
    - Scale
    - Data sensitivity
    - Business criticality

Waiver:
  Format: WAIVER-NNN
  Fields: Gate, Reason, Owner, Expiration, Risk, Approval
  Rules:
    [WVR1] Waiver MUST have Reason, Owner, Expiration, Risk, Approval.
    [WVR2] Waiver is temporary; expired waivers re-trigger gate.
    [WVR3] Waiver does not bypass gate permanently.
    [WVR4] Waiver MUST be recorded in graph.

Evidence:
  Every gate result MUST include:
    - Who ran the gate
    - What was tested
    - When it was run
    - Why it was run
    - Result (PASS/FAIL/BLOCKED/etc.)
    - Evidence artifact

  EvidenceRules:
    [EV1] Every gate MUST produce evidence.
    [EV2] Evidence MUST be immutable after gate completion.
    [EV3] Evidence MUST be linkable from graph.
    [EV4] Evidence MUST be retrievable for audit.

Rules:
  [GP1]  Gates are adaptive, not one-size-fits-all.
  [GP2]  Gate selection is based on project context.
  [GP3]  Every gate MUST have Condition + Evidence + Threshold + Owner + Decision.
  [GP4]  Gate failure blocks subsequent gates.
  [GP5]  Critical gates are hard blockers.
  [EX1]  SKIPPED ≠ WAIVED.
  [EX2]  Waivers require explicit approval.
  [EX3]  Waivers have expiration dates.
  [EX4]  Expired waivers MUST be renewed or gate re-run.

